\newlabel{fig:define}{{1}{1}{Conventional person ReID vs. our st-ReID. (a) Retrieval results of the conventional person ReID. Without the help of spatial-temporal information, it is difficult for the conventional ReID to deal with the appearance ambiguity (red boxes denote false alarms). (b) Retrieval results of our st-ReID. With spatial-temporal information, st-ReID can eliminate irrelevant images. Besides, spatial-temporal information (camera ID and timestamp) of st-ReID widely exists in video surveillance and can be easily collected without any manual annotation. (Best viewed in color)}{}{}}
